[DESCRIPTION]: The function takes an input string and modifies every odd-indexed character by replacing it with the next character in the alphabet, except when the character is 'z' or 'Z', in which case it remains unchanged.

[CODE]:
```python
def approximate_function(s):
    result = ""
    for i, c in enumerate(s):
        if i % 2 == 1 and c.lower() != 'z':
            result += chr(ord(c) + 1)
        else:
            result += c
    return result
```
